> battle pretty pointless if the creature you're meleeing with has any
> substantial hit points as it wears out before the creature's dead. [...]

Protection is cumulative to a certain degree, so you may cast it a couple
of times before combat. Protection just increases your AC value, it grants
no immunity, it will give you an advantage immediately in a timely manner.
Its purpose is neither to become immune nor to fight enemies that are far
beyond your heroes capabilities; one should still flee from such monsters.
If you cannot kill a monster in 10(!) turns, which is really a lot, flee!
In other words; protection as currently implemented is quite balanced,
while extending this practically non-expiring feature would clearly make
it overpowered; if it would last 100-200 turns, as you propose, one could
constantly cast it, because in that time span mana would be recovered as
well. I found protection to be quite helpful, especially in the early game.
Just don't think you'll become a superman and get overconfident, but the
difference in AC can save your b.., life.

